hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24304","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from him, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mujalid informed us, Amir informed me, from Farwah ibn Musayk al-Muradi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Were you distressed by your day and the day of Hamdan, I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, the perishing of family and kin, he said: Yet it is better for whoever of you is God-fearing."
